MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone,

I was wondering if anyone else had come across the situation where the accelerometer calibration error calculation was not complete for a participants data? We recently had this case, but it was not something I have come across before. To be clear, as the calibration calculation was not complete, we do not know if the accelerometer was, or was not appropriately calibrated during data collection. All data seems inline with normal ranges etc.

If anyone has come across this before, how did you treat this data - i.e., did you use or disregard the data?

If you haven't come across this before, do you have a recommendation on how you would treat this data.

Many thanks,

Gareth

From u9f58683bb92d4062 at groups.google.com  Tue Jan 28 12:38:12 2025
